0,Austronesian languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austronesian_languages,"The Austronesian languages are a language family widely spoken throughout Maritime Southeast Asia, parts of Mainland Southeast Asia, Madagascar, the islands of the Pacific Ocean and Taiwan. They are spoken by about 386 million people.","Malay, Bacanese",Austronesian
1,Malay trade and creole languages - Wikipedia,https://web.archive.org/web/20230306021902/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malay_trade_and_creole_languages,"Bacanese Malay is a Malayic isolect spoken in Bacan Island and its surroundings, south of Halmahera , North Maluku .Gorap is lexically 85% Malay, but has many Ternate words as well, and word order differs from both Austronesian and Halmahera languages .","Malay, Bacanese",Austronesian
